{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SanjqgCUFQj9f6sL94tSGV","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/2fad7a23bedb14aad623504b880973f9da21a136b80a7bf0d0a6a4401314c09c.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task host-tooling: Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"host\\\",\\\"scripts/run-tp2.sh\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:ae2073776d62dfbb3deda47df09b2818a7f1c433285bd076fb130ddf2ed75a95\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"for f in host/*.sh scripts/run-tp2.sh; do bash -n \\\"$f\\\"; done && grep -q 'PYTHONHASHSEED=0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'thunderbolt0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'ExecStopPost' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && ! grep -q 'WantedBy' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v\"],\"description\":\"Env doctrine present, units teardown-safe, all scripts syntax-clean, host tests pass.\",\"id\":\"host-doctrine\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"host\",\"scripts/run-tp2.sh\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"One command stands the pair service; one command tears it down; failure cannot strand ranks\",\"First light produces the four receipts the ladder grades\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Write the host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh per spec claims 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5 and 6.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4, #r6), composing the disciplines in specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 5 and specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 5. host/fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0; PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85; HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1; inductor and triton cache dirs under the state directory, never tmpfs; NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME set ONLY to the Thunderbolt rails that carry a routable /30 IP (rail 0 thunderbolt0/10.99.0.x is guaranteed; rail 1 thunderbolt1 is trained-but-IP-unconfigured today per dotfiles modules/lowlat-cluster.nix and MUST NOT be listed until it has a peer IP — a peerless link-local rail in the list hangs RCCL bootstrap; the env file computes this from `ip -br addr` at write time and logs which rails it chose, rather than hardcoding both); NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 UNCONDITIONALLY (an ibverbs device now exists on the rails from the pre-arm bake; without this pin RCCL autodetects verbs and silently rides unproven RDMA — sockets are the transport of record until the attended morning A/B, evidence host/rdma/ab-protocol.md); VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_; VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1; a loud comment forbidding exports of engine defaults read through is-set probes. host/fn-cluster-up.sh: podman on both nodes (worker over ssh on the wire), distributed head on the coordinator and worker join, worker python pool capped small, a hard two-GPU gate before serve, then the serve process at tensor-parallel size 2 with eager execution, model directory /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8, served name flashnext; reap stranded serve processes before start and gate on zero residue. host/fn-cluster-down.sh: idempotent teardown both nodes. host/fn-preflight.sh: byte-diff of both ranks' FN_ env, latency-hold device read on both ends, per-rail link-speed record, round-trip probe on both rails. host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service: oneshot, RemainAfterExit, ExecStopPost teardown, no install section. scripts/run-tp2.sh: preflight, up, two greedy 300-token completions byte-compared, residency read after 50 warmed decode tokens (GTT per rank from sysfs plus process RSS plus table page-cache residency), fidelity capture (fixed-prompt losses and frontier logits under results/), then a 262144-context probe, writing receipts tp2.json, residency.json, fidelity.json, context.json per the receipts-verify.py schema. Extend tests/test_repo_invariants.py-adjacent coverage with tests/test_host_tooling.py asserting the env file carries the doctrine lines and unit files carry ExecStopPost and no WantedBy install. Boundaries: touch only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, and tests/.\",\"id\":\"host-tooling\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\",\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/stage-weights.sh\",\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d\",\"title\":\"Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"ff1731c6c5886748faa13231e2f6012936bfb5dd\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-74023f65ddcc/host-tooling\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"host\",\"scripts/run-tp2.sh\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f\",\"taskId\":\"host-tooling\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/74023f65ddcc/host-tooling\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":0,\"recheckedCursor\":0,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c36b10f-f6a6-469d-ae79-b7ca895bdd12","uuid":"2f4c1b56-028c-474b-a55b-a1054bc68ed0","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:20:29.052Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/2fad7a23bedb14aad623504b880973f9da21a136b80a7bf0d0a6a4401314c09c.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task host-tooling: Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner. Commit the c