{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYDY9fRsK8FsAZ38DTnb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HWkyMCbo6bA5tXh68dsuJH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add host/fn-env.sh host/fn-cluster-down.sh tests/test_host_tooling.py && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nhost-tooling: the reap gate aborted the bring-up on every clean night\n\nreap_serve_node ended in `pgrep -f 'bin/[v]llm serve' | wc -l`. pgrep exits\n1 when nothing matches — the HEALTHY case — and under fn-cluster-up.sh's\n`set -euo pipefail` that 1 propagates out of the pipeline, out of the\n`residue=\"$(reap_serve_node)\"` command substitution, and into `set -e`.\n\nSo the one command that stands the pair died at its FIRST step, exit 1 with\nan empty stderr, on exactly the nights no serve process was stranded. The\nzero-residue gate never logged, the image never shipped, ray never started.\nA night with a stale husk would have proceeded; a clean night could not.\n\nCount by branching on the pid list instead of piping it. Same fix in\nfn-cluster-down.sh's copy of the helper: teardown runs without `set -e`\ntoday, so it was not fatal there, but the two helpers must not drift into\ndifferent failure semantics. bench/run-matrix.sh already guarded its calls\nwith `|| true` and is unaffected either way.\n\nBoth new tests EXECUTE the helper under real `set -euo pipefail` with pgrep\nstubbed — no live process is ever signalled — and both fail against the\npre-fix file: the healthy case with the same silent empty-stderr abort.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit status --porcelain; echo \"porcelain exit=$? (empty above = clean)\"; git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the fix and confirm clean tree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":804,"cache_read_input_tokens":82411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":804},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c36b10f-f6a6-469d-ae79-b7ca895bdd12","uuid":"48e4a44c-3fa4-44f7-aa06-40c86296a527","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:23:56.445Z","request_id":"req_011CeYDY8rZNumvtCY9gKiZy"}
